%%{init: {"flowchart": {"htmlLabels": false, "useMaxWidth": true, "nodeSpacing": 20, "rankSpacing": 28}, "themeVariables": {"fontSize": "3.2px"}}}%%
flowchart TD
    earth["1. VERIFIED: Earth walking baseline<br/><br/>Pretrained rough-H1 checkpoint loaded; no PPO<br/>training performed in this project.<br/><br/>Body-forward command: 0.5 m/s. Reproducible<br/>Earth spawn and heading.<br/><br/>Earth-8: six seconds recorded after one second<br/>of settling. Zero resets; all terrain<br/>measurements remained finite.<br/><br/>This verifies a short walk, not general<br/>walking stability across repeated trials."]
    contact["2. IMPLEMENTED: Local Earth ground<br/><br/>Trail-following collision patch: 4 × 6.5 m,<br/>sampled every 5 cm.<br/><br/>Physics and height sensing use the same<br/>triangle mesh. Separate rocks and foliage<br/>remain visual-only.<br/><br/>Only the local walking corridor has ground<br/>collision; distant scenery adds no contact<br/>dynamics."]
    camera["3. VERIFIED: Recording and smooth<br/>orbit<br/><br/>Six-second H.264 MP4, playable on Mac.<br/>Original recordings are preserved.<br/><br/>Camera position AND aim are smoothed. Stronger<br/>vertical damping suppresses footstep bounce<br/>while following travel.<br/><br/>Lighting startup remains intermittent. Inspect<br/>rendered robot and ground for every recording;<br/>retry if lighting fails."]
    mars["4. CURRENT MARS: Rigid terrain only<br/><br/>Canyon scenery, lighting and rigid collision<br/>mesh are present. Mars gravity: −3.71 m/s².<br/><br/>Existing collider: roughly 47 × 47 m with only<br/>128 triangles. Too coarse for detailed local<br/>foot contacts.<br/><br/>Atmospheric drag, dust and loose regolith are<br/>not implemented.<br/><br/>CURRENT FOCUS: validate local Mars<br/>environmental physics before connecting the<br/>walking policy."]
    route["5. NEXT: Define the Mars route<br/><br/>Fix spawn, heading and initial velocities.<br/>Remove randomized starts for repeatable<br/>environment tests.<br/><br/>Reference command: 0.5 m/s for 6 seconds gives<br/>3 m of commanded travel, not guaranteed actual<br/>distance.<br/><br/>Add settling travel and margins for footsteps,<br/>recovery and the height scanner.<br/><br/>Choose exact Mars bounds from its route; do<br/>not automatically reuse the Earth crop."]
    crop["6. PLANNED: Build local Mars terrain<br/><br/>Recover source terrain and restore builder<br/>inputs from provenance or history where<br/>needed.<br/><br/>Replace the coarse collider with a detailed<br/>surface matching the visible route.<br/><br/>Limit contact computation to that corridor<br/>plus margins; keep distant scenery<br/>visual-only.<br/><br/>Validate alignment and complete coverage. Do<br/>not activate soil only under instantaneous<br/>footprints: surrounding soil must support<br/>contact."]
    soil["7. PLANNED: Add loose regolith<br/><br/>Proposed design: a shallow deformable soil<br/>layer over a rigid terrain base.<br/><br/>Model load support, sinkage, sideways<br/>resistance and soil displacement within the<br/>local corridor.<br/><br/>Lower friction alone approximates sliding; it<br/>cannot reproduce sinking or footprints.<br/><br/>Select and validate the contact method. This<br/>is not yet an implemented or calibrated<br/>regolith solver."]
    sensing["8. PLANNED: Match terrain sensing<br/><br/>The current height scanner reads a static<br/>mesh; it does not automatically see soil<br/>deformation.<br/><br/>Update surface measurements as soil changes.<br/>The policy must sense the surface its feet<br/>actually touch.<br/><br/>Check for missed rays and preserve scanner<br/>coverage throughout the route."]
    foot["9. PLANNED: Loaded-foot validation<br/><br/>Test WITHOUT the walking policy first. Press,<br/>settle and slide a loaded foot on the local<br/>soil.<br/><br/>Measure contact forces, sinkage, slip and<br/>displaced soil.<br/><br/>Check timestep stability and simulation cost.<br/>Calibrate parameters before claiming realistic<br/>regolith behavior."]
    drag["10. PLANNED: Atmospheric forces<br/><br/>No Earth aerodynamic model currently exists to<br/>reduce. Body damping is already zero.<br/><br/>Add explicit air resistance using Mars<br/>atmospheric density and velocity relative to<br/>wind.<br/><br/>Keep motor and joint damping separate: those<br/>describe the robot, not atmospheric drag.<br/><br/>Validate the small aerodynamic forces<br/>independently of soil contact."]
    dust["11. PLANNED: Local dust plumes<br/><br/>Emit dust near foot impacts and sliding. Bound<br/>particle count, lifetime and active region to<br/>control cost.<br/><br/>Distinguish visual airborne dust from<br/>mechanically interacting soil particles.<br/><br/>Visual dust alone will not affect this policy:<br/>its inputs are robot state and terrain<br/>heights, not camera images."]
    gate["12. PLANNED: Environment validation<br/><br/>Repeat isolated tests with soil, air forces<br/>and dust enabled together.<br/><br/>Check contacts, changing surface measurements,<br/>route boundaries and runtime performance.<br/><br/>Record parameters and distinguish<br/>approximations from calibrated physics.<br/><br/>Only proceed to policy integration after these<br/>environment checks pass."]
    playback["13. THEN: Run the policy on Mars<br/><br/>Use the same pretrained checkpoint with<br/>reproducible starts on the validated local<br/>environment.<br/><br/>Measure actual travel, slips, sinkage and<br/>falls.<br/><br/>Add stop-on-fall and route-exit handling. The<br/>runner currently counts resets; it does not<br/>yet stop on every fall.<br/><br/>Do not hide failures by continuing through<br/>episode resets."]
    compare["14. LATER: Compare Earth and Mars<br/><br/>Define a shared target distance and explicit<br/>success criteria.<br/><br/>Run 100 seeded trajectories per environment.<br/>Log actual distance, simulation time, slips<br/>and falls.<br/><br/>Export outcomes and comparison recordings.<br/><br/>Control steps are not footsteps. Counting 5–10<br/>footsteps requires contact-event logic, which<br/>remains to be implemented."]

    earth --> contact --> camera --> mars --> route --> crop --> soil --> sensing --> foot --> drag --> dust --> gate --> playback --> compare

